# Curriculum core

Security is maintaining **invariants under adversarial conditions**. Every control is derived from a threat and a required property. Every claimed property needs evidence. Preventive controls are paired with detection and recovery where appropriate.

The path is **builder-first and spiral**, not a waterfall and not a rotating Top 10. Learners ship vertical slices of **SecureCollab**, then revisit earlier models when identity, persistence, mobile, deployment, or operating assumptions change.

Offensive technique exists only to expose causes, validate impact, and verify repairs. It is not the organizing goal.

Canonical source: `secure-application-engineering-curriculum-blueprint.md`. Module order and gates in `content/progress/STATUS.yaml`. Do not skip phases. Phase 8 (mobile) may be postponed for a web/API-only milestone. Electives open after Phase 7.

Saltzer–Schroeder principles plus modern additions (attack surface, blast radius, distrust external data/clients, explicit state, revocation, dependencies as attack surface) organize teaching. Framework defaults are not application guarantees.
